            "body": "> This sounds reasonable and desirable to me, but please open this at vim/vim -- this is shared code, and we don't want to diverge needlessly. It's better to let Vim discuss and decide on this and for us to simply port their patch.\n\nThat makes some sense, but it would be nice to document this practice somewhere in CONTRIBUTING.md, as it's not exactly obvious for newer contributors. Somehow I thought that Neovim moves away from compatibility with Vim.",
